omprobar si los contratos [1], [2], [3] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en otros años. Analizar si los contratos al límite coinciden con presupuestos cerrados o circunstancias particulares.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 143 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 19.6 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 7.3, with a 95% confidence interval of 5.6 to 9.5. December accounts for 9% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 5% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 86 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,354 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December does not indicate improper activity. Similar trends could result from seasonal demand or budgetary planning. The number of contracts near the limit does not prove violations, as market rates or fixed budgets might influence amounts.\nWhat can be checked: Check the dates and values of contracts awarded in December to see if they align with usual patterns. Review the services provided by awardee A to determine if multiple contracts serve the same need. Examine if contracts [1], [2], and [3] were part of a larger procurement strategy.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["p0pLKyfrVPE4NavIWzMcHA%3D%3D","aeX8xevbBpmOUi78BmzhOQ%3D%3D","YwlcWMnKXnq8ebB%2FXTwy0A%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}